{
  "about": "Real answers of the Didit verification API to POST /v1/events/batch/, recorded on 2026-10-12 from a local run of the service with this package's own build sending the requests. Tokens are replaced by the label of the credential state they had (valid, expired, used_up, revoked, origin_bound, session_only, monitoring_disabled, unknown). too_many was sent raw: the SDK never puts more than 500 events in one request. Returned event_uuid values are sanitized, not original service identifiers: distinct values receive sequential synthetic UUIDs with prefix 00000000-0000-4000-8000- and a 12-digit hexadecimal counter starting at 1 in first-occurrence order. Repeated values keep the same replacement, including accepted/replayed pairs. Request labels (rec-*, web-1) are synthetic test inputs. Response shapes, indexes, outcomes, errors and all other recorded fields are unchanged.",
